<title>SWEDEN: P&amp;U launches Nicorette inhaler.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U launches Nicorette inhaler.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S.-Swedish drug company Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn said on Friday that it is launching in Denmark a Nicorette inhaler to be used by people trying to give up smoking.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement that this would be the first launch but it had plans to offer the new product across Europe and internationally.</p>
<p>The Nicorette inhaler is based on the same principles as the company's Nicorette chewing gum, plasters and spray.</p>
<p>It said the inhaler had taken several years to develop and had been through six clinical stuides with 1,440 smokers in Denmark, Sweden, and the United States.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
</text>
